{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`BindingStore` is the authoritative local-id ↔ Jira identity aggregate and must remain so, but its 799-line module now owns byte persistence, live/reverse lifecycle policy, retirement, recovery, peer-state delegates, comment identity, and GET rotation. New safety rules have no cohesive owner, and production code mutates an inner entry returned by the shallow `all_bindings()` compatibility query. A mechanical split could regress hard-won crash, index-lag, identity, serialization, and selective-publication behavior.\n\n## Outcome\nKeep one public `BindingStore` facade and existing import/method compatibility while extracting three internal owners: a byte-preserving repository/unit-of-work, lifecycle policy, and incomplete-operation recovery. Typed views remain open over the original dictionaries so unknown fields and exact JSON behavior survive. Add the approved journal-free retirement completion rule: a durable tombstone is authoritative intent, and a live forward/reverse pair is removed only when tombstone, forward, and reverse identities all agree. Only explicit `unretire` revokes that intent; automatic liveness observations never resurrect a tombstoned identity.\n\n## Delivery slices\n1. Extract repository/unit-of-work persistence behind the facade with byte, fault-cut, corruption, rotation-order, and selective-publication regression oracles; establish ADR 0099 with the complete approved target design.\n2. Extract lifecycle policy and add narrow facade operations so new production code no longer needs mutation-through-query while `all_bindings()` remains shallow-compatible.\n3. Extract recovery, cut the live caller to the narrow mutation seam, complete exact-match interrupted retirements before remote issue observation, and finalize ADR 0099 to describe the realized behavior.\n\n## Architectural constraints\n- Preserve `peer_state.py`, `get_rotation.py`, pending → confirmed → reversible retired lifecycle, numeric-ID re-key, comment identity, and the existing five-file selective tickets publication.\n- Preserve unknown fields, `indent=2`, sorted keys, trailing newline, legacy additive reads, and unchanged-pass byte/HEAD idempotency.\n- Corrupt live state still fails closed; retired/rotation/alert/commit failure behavior changes only when this plan names it.\n- Construction, load, check, dry-run, preview, selection, and filtered operations do not perform recovery writes.\n- Live recovery runs after configuration snapshot/preflight and exclusive lock/staleness validation but before remote issue fetch, binding walk, differ, or lifecycle mutation. This ordering prevents an upgraded pass from interleaving new liveness evidence with completion.\n- In a historical overlap, stale `absent_404_count`, automatic 200/`clear_absent`, or same-key confirm cannot revoke the durable tombstone; only explicit `unretire` removes it and thereby eliminates the completion candidate.\n- No general journal, format migration, eager rewrite, broad `git add -A`, deep-copy change to `all_bindings()`, or new identity writer.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nEach slice is an internal facade delegation with unchanged stored formats and public signatures. A slice can be reverted independently to the preceding facade implementation. The exact-match repair is additive and idempotent: disabling its pre-observation live-operation call restores the prior detectable overlap without rewriting coherent stores. Rollback never deletes a remote issue or implies automatic unretire.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Existing `BindingStore` imports, signatures, shallow `all_bindings()` behavior, unknown-field preservation, and exact serialization remain compatible through direct-loader and public-facade tests.\n- [x] Repository fault-cut tests preserve current rotation-before-live ordering, per-file atomic replacement, selective five-file publication, and explicit failure outcomes.\n- [x] Lifecycle tests preserve both-index identity guards, pending/confirmed/retired rules, 404 grace/reset, immutable-ID re-key, tombstone suppression/unretire, and append-only comment identity.\n- [x] Recovery tests prove keyed/keyless create recovery and exact-match retirement completion are idempotent; repair runs before remote observation, identities must agree, and ambiguity/replace failure safety-aborts.\n- [x] Automatic liveness signals do not override durable retirement intent; explicit `unretire` removes the tombstone and prevents completion.\n- [x] Load/check/dry-run/preview/selection/filtered tests prove zero recovery writes; only a validated write-bearing operation may repair an interrupted retirement.\n- [x] ADR 0099 identifies preserved behavior, the intentional repair behavior, explicit-unretire reversal, pre-observation ordering, rollback, and the prohibition on broad tickets-branch staging."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787169965813857001,"uuid":"c342abcf-c069-4ad2-80a8-8f5fff015b8b"}